UID:605-1784973600-1784980800@baltimoreindiegames.com
SUMMARY:Summer Hike
DESCRIPTION:We’re hiking the Buzzards Rock Trail Loop in Patapsco Valley State Park!\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/maryland/buzzards-rock-trail-loop \nPlease meet us at the Buzzards Rock Trailhead on S Hilltop Road: https://maps.app.goo.gl/zSeiz2nGWGPvHnaz6\nYou don’t need to drive into the park itself\, which has a paid entrance fee. You can park at the trailhead instead. \nBring water and comfortable hiking shoes. It’s a 2.5 mile loop that should take 1 – 1.5 hours. \nRain or shine\, so check the weather and bring a rain jacket if needed.
URL:https://baltimoreindiegames.com/event/summer-hike-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260725T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260725T190000
DTSTAMP:20260623T145843Z
CREATED:20260623T145843Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260623T145843Z
UID:592-1784979000-1785006000@baltimoreindiegames.com
SUMMARY:Smithsonian SAAM Arcade 2026
DESCRIPTION:Experience the creative world of gaming at SAAM Arcade\, a day-long celebration of video games as an artistic medium that expands the way we tell and experience stories. A centerpiece of the event is the Indie Showcase that this year highlights a selection of games brought to you by women in the field of video game development. This is a special opportunity to play games and talk with the designers and coders who created them. Triforce Quartet will perform\, and console games and classic arcade games will be available to enjoy all day courtesy of MAGFest. \nNote: the first 90 minutes are designated quiet hours\, with reduced noise to ensure that a portion of the program is sensory friendly. Headphones will be available to borrow all day. \nSchedule:\n11:30 a.m. – 1 p.m. – Quiet hours\n1:30 p.m. – Triforce Quartet performance\n4:30 p.m. – Triforce Quartet performance\n6:50 p.m. – Last call for game play\n7 p.m. – Program ends
URL:https://baltimoreindiegames.com/event/smithsonian-saam-arcade-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T200000
DTSTAMP:20260719T151913Z
CREATED:20260719T151913Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260719T151913Z
UID:642-1785263400-1785268800@baltimoreindiegames.com
SUMMARY:IGDA DC Speaker Night: Joy Horvath (Unity)
DESCRIPTION:This is an online speaker night hosted on our discord: https://discord.gg/upXHsdDuQg \nJoy Horvath is the founder of Unity’s “Elevate” career-development initiative. In that role\, she’s conducted in-depth investigations of the opportunities for entry into the gamedev profession at every level. Now a Unity Senior Advocate and Livestream Host\, Joy will be talking to us about the state of the industry as a source of employment for entry-level gamedevs. This is a chance to hear some straight talk from an insider on what the options and likelihoods are for “breaking in.”
URL:https://baltimoreindiegames.com/event/igda-dc-speaker-night-joy-horvath-unity/
END:VEVENT
